@startuml
title Invalid input: zero ingredient quantity and recovery
autonumber

participant "<u>MishMash</u>" as App
participant "parser: Parser" as Parser

App -> Parser : parseCommand(input)
activate Parser
note over Parser
  input = add-recipe n/Rice cal/200 p/4 c/45 f/1 i/Rice:0g
  parseNamedCommand dispatch is condensed.
end note
Parser -> Parser : parseAddRecipeCommand(arguments)
activate Parser
Parser -> Parser : parseAddRecipe(arguments)
activate Parser
Parser -> Parser : collectRecipeArguments(arguments, fields, ingredients)
activate Parser
note right of Parser : Earlier single-value fields have been collected locally.
Parser -> Parser : readArgument("i", "Rice:0g", fields, ingredients)
activate Parser
Parser -> Parser : parseIngredient("Rice:0g")
activate Parser
Parser --> Parser : throws IllegalArgumentException(\n"Ingredient quantity must be greater than zero.")
deactivate Parser
Parser --> Parser : propagates IllegalArgumentException
deactivate Parser
Parser --> Parser : propagates IllegalArgumentException
deactivate Parser
Parser --> Parser : propagates IllegalArgumentException
deactivate Parser
note right of Parser
  parseAddRecipeCommand catches the exception,
  appends ADD_RECIPE_USAGE, and preserves the cause.
end note
Parser --> Parser : throws MishMashException(message + usage, cause)
deactivate Parser
Parser --> App : propagates MishMashException
deactivate Parser
note over App
  executeCommand catches MishMashException.
end note
App -> App : <u>displayError(exception)</u>
activate App
note right of App
  Print "Error: " and the message with add-recipe usage.
  No extra COMMAND_USAGE is printed because
  the message already contains "Format: ".
end note
App --> App : return
deactivate App
note over App : Control returns to readCommands.
App -> App : <u>displayCommandPrompt()</u>
activate App
App --> App : return
deactivate App

legend bottom
  Dashed exception messages describe exceptional control flow, not normal return values.
  Underlining denotes the class participant and static application operations.
  No GroceryItem, Recipe, or AddRecipeCommand is constructed for this example.
  The recipe book is not accessed; the session accepts another input line.
endlegend
@enduml
